  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The user's long prompt (or document) is loaded into a **REPL environment** (like a Jupyter notebook) as a variable, typically named",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The LLM is prompted to solve the task by **writing Python code** that interacts with this",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The RLM framework is highly modular and extensible:",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Results bubble up and are synthesized",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "This turns context management into **code generation**, which LLMs are increasingly good at",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The codebase is open and welcoming to contributions—now is an excellent time to experiment and build upon this paradigm",
